{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 39, :comments ["And if any beast of which you may eat die, etc. — but if it was slaughtered it is not a nevelah, even if it is found to be a terefah; but regarding the carcass of an unclean beast Scripture did not mention death, because even if it was slaughtered it is a nevelah and imparts impurity. And the Sages derived:" "Of the beast — some beasts impart impurity and some do not. This is a terefah that was slaughtered: it is clean from the status of nevelah."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 11, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:48:42.037127505Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}